# Angular Conventions (Pierre's style)

- Standalone components only; declare dependencies in `imports`.
- Use `templateUrl` + `styleUrl` (not inline templates/styles).
- Selectors: `app-{name}`; files: `{name}.component.ts` in kebab-case folders.
- Pages: `src/app/pages/manor/{room}/`; shared UI: `src/app/components/ui/`.
- Import order: Angular core → Angular common/forms/router → local components.
- Room pages include `TopBarComponent` with `backLink` and `pageText` where applicable.
- Route `title` in French; paths match existing `app.routes.ts` patterns (French segments).
- Prefer `@if` / `@for` (with `track`); do not introduce new `*ngIf` / `*ngFor`.
- Prefer `input()` / `output()` over `@Input()` / `@Output()`.
- Prefer `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` on new and touched components.
- Prefer typed arrays / interfaces over loose `object` and the `keyvalue` pipe.
- Prefer stable class-level arrays over allocating in templates (`[].constructor(n)`).
- Assets: `assets/images/...`, `assets/sound/...` (no leading `/` — base-href safe).
- In-app navigation: `routerLink` / `[routerLink]`, never absolute `href` to app routes.
